title: "NVMe Emulation"
source: "system/devices/nvme.rst"
---

# NVMe Emulation

QEMU provides NVMe emulation through the `nvme`, `nvme-ns` and `nvme-subsys` devices.

## Adding NVMe Devices

### Controller Emulation

The QEMU emulated NVMe controller implements version 1.4 of the NVM Express specification. Limitations:

- Accounting numbers in the SMART/Health log page are reset when the device is power cycled
- Interrupt Coalescing is not supported and is disabled by default

Simplest way to attach an NVMe controller:
```
-drive file=nvm.img,if=none,id=nvm
-device nvme,serial=deadbeef,drive=nvm
```

### Optional Parameters

| Parameter | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `max_ioqpairs=UINT32` | 64 | Maximum I/O queue pairs |
| `msix_qsize=UINT16` | 65 | Number of MSI-X vectors |
| `mdts=UINT8` | 7 | Maximum Data Transfer Size |
| `use-intel-id` | off | Use unallocated Intel ID |
| `ocp` | off | Enable OCP features |
| `model` | "QEMU NVMe Ctrl" | Override model (max 40 chars) |
| `firmware-version` | QEMU version | Override firmware version (max 8 chars) |

### Additional Namespaces

Use the `nvme-ns` device for multiple namespaces:
```
-device nvme,id=nvme-ctrl-0,serial=deadbeef
-drive file=nvm-1.img,if=none,id=nvm-1
-device nvme-ns,drive=nvm-1
```

Namespace parameters: `nsid`, `uuid`, `nguid`, `eui64`, `bus`.

### NVM Subsystems

Link to `nvme-subsys` for shared namespaces and multipath I/O:
```
-device nvme-subsys,id=nvme-subsys-0,nqn=subsys0
-device nvme,serial=deadbeef,subsys=nvme-subsys-0
```

## Optional Features

### Controller Memory Buffer
- `cmb_size_mb=UINT32` (default: 0)
- `legacy-cmb` (default: off)

### Simple Copy (TP 4065)
Parameters: `mssrl` (default: 128), `mcl` (default: 128), `msrc` (default: 127)

### Zoned Namespaces (TP 4053)
Set `zoned=on` on `nvme-ns`. Parameters: `zoned.zone_size`, `zoned.zone_capacity`, `zoned.descr_ext_size`, `zoned.cross_read`, `zoned.max_active`, `zoned.max_open`, `zoned.zasl`.

### Flexible Data Placement (TP4146)
Configure `fdp=on` on subsystem. Parameters: `fdp.nrg`, `fdp.nruh`, `fdp.runs`.

### Metadata
- `ms=UINT16` (default: 0) - Metadata bytes per LBA
- `mset=UINT8` (default: 0) - Set to 1 for extended LBAs

### End-to-End Data Protection
- `pi=UINT8` - Protection type (1, 2, or 3)
- `pil=UINT8` - Protection info location
- `pif=UINT8` - Guard format (0=16bit, 2=64bit)

### SR-IOV (Experimental)
Parameters: `sriov_max_vfs`, `sriov_vq_flexible`, `sriov_vi_flexible`, `sriov_max_vi_per_vf`, `sriov_max_vq_per_vf`.
ENDOFFILE
