title: "USB Emulation"
source: "system/devices/usb.rst"
---

# USB Emulation

QEMU can emulate a PCI UHCI, OHCI, EHCI or XHCI USB controller. You can plug virtual USB devices or real host USB devices.

## USB Controllers

### XHCI Controller Support

XHCI is recommended for any OS released around 2010 or later. It supports USB 1.1, USB 2.0 and USB 3.0 devices:

```
qemu-system-x86_64 -device qemu-xhci
```

### EHCI Controller Support

Supports USB 2.0 devices. Can be used standalone or with companion controllers (UHCI, OHCI) for USB 1.1 devices.

### Companion Controller Support

UHCI and OHCI controllers can attach to a USB bus created by EHCI using `masterbus` and `firstport` properties.

## Connecting USB Devices

Available USB devices:

| Device | Description |
|---|---|
| `usb-mouse` | Virtual Mouse |
| `usb-tablet` | Absolute coordinate pointer |
| `usb-storage,drive=drive_id` | Mass storage |
| `usb-uas` | USB attached SCSI |
| `usb-bot` | Bulk-only transport storage |
| `usb-mtp,rootdir=dir` | Media transfer protocol |
| `usb-host` | Host device passthrough |
| `usb-wacom-tablet` | Wacom PenPartner tablet |
| `usb-kbd` | Standard USB keyboard |
| `usb-serial,chardev=id` | Serial converter (FTDI FT232BM) |
| `usb-braille,chardev=id` | Braille device |
| `usb-net[,netdev=id]` | Network adapter (CDC/RNDIS) |
| `usb-ccid` | Smartcard reader |
| `usb-audio` | USB audio device |
| `canokey` | FIDO2/OpenPGP/PIV key |

## Physical Port Addressing

Use the `port` property to specify physical port. UHCI has 2 root ports, EHCI has 6, emulated hub has 8.

## Host USB Devices on Linux

`usb-host` properties:
- `hostbus=<nr>`, `hostaddr=<nr>`, `hostport=<str>`, `vendorid=<hexnr>`, `productid=<hexnr>`

### Reset Behavior
- `guest-reset=false` - No reset allowed
- `guest-reset=true,guest-resets-all=false` - One reset allowed (default)
- `guest-reset=true,guest-resets-all=true` - Free reset

## Recording USB Transfers

```
-device usb-mouse,pcap=mouse.pcap
```
ENDOFFILE
