# Microblaze-V Generic Board (amd-microblaze-v-generic)

The AMD MicroBlaze V processor is a soft-core RISC-V processor IP for AMD adaptive SoCs and FPGAs. It is based on the 32-bit (or 64-bit) RISC-V instruction set architecture (ISA) and contains interfaces compatible with the classic MicroBlaze V processor.

More information: https://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug1629-microblaze-v-user-guide/MicroBlaze-V-Architecture

## Supported Devices

- timer
- uartlite
- uart16550
- emaclite
- timer2
- axi emac
- axi dma

## Core Configuration

- RV32I base integer instruction set
- "Zicsr" Control and Status register instructions
- "Zifencei" instruction-fetch
- Extensions: m, a, f, c

## Running

Example command line for launching mainline U-boot (xilinx_mbv32_defconfig):

```bash
qemu-system-riscv32 -M amd-microblaze-v-generic \
  -display none \
  -device loader,addr=0x80000000,file=u-boot-spl.bin,cpu-num=0 \
  -device loader,addr=0x80200000,file=u-boot.img \
  -serial mon:stdio \
  -device loader,addr=0x83000000,file=system.dtb \
  -m 2g
```
ENDOFFILE)
