# RISC-V Processors by MIPS (boston-aia)

RISC-V processors developed by MIPS support Boston-aia board model. The board model supports up to 64 harts with MIPS CPS, MIPS GCR, MIPS CPC, AIA plic, and AIA clint devices.

## Running Linux Kernel

```bash
qemu-system-riscv64 -cpu mips-p8700 \
  -m 2G -M boston-aia \
  -smp 8,cores=4,threads=2 -kernel fw_payload.bin \
  -drive file=rootfs.ext2,format=raw -serial stdio
```
ENDOFFILE)
