# Shakti C Reference Platform (shakti_c)

Shakti C Reference Platform is a reference platform based on arty a7 100t for the Shakti SoC. Shakti C is a 64bit RV64GCSUN processor core.

## Supported Devices

- 1 C-class core
- Core Level Interruptor (CLINT)
- Platform-Level Interrupt Controller (PLIC)
- 1 UART

## Boot Options

The `shakti_c` machine can start using the standard `-bios` functionality for loading baremetal applications or OpenSBI.

## Shakti SDK

```bash
git clone https://gitlab.com/behindbytes/shakti-sdk.git
cd shakti-sdk
make software PROGRAM=loopback TARGET=artix7_100t
```

Run the UART example:

```bash
qemu-system-riscv64 -M shakti_c -nographic \
   -bios path/to/shakti_sdk_qemu/loopback.shakti
```

## OpenSBI

```bash
git clone https://github.com/riscv/opensbi.git -b v0.9
cd opensbi
export CROSS_COMPILE=riscv64-unknown-elf-
export FW_FDT_PATH=./shakti.dtb
make PLATFORM=generic
```

```bash
qemu-system-riscv64 -M shakti_c -nographic \
   -bios path/to/fw_payload.elf
```
ENDOFFILE)
