source: system/s390x/protvirt.rst
---

# Protected Virtualization on s390x

Protected Virtual Machines (PVMs) have encrypted memory and registers, inaccessible to the hypervisor. At rest, PVMs are encrypted and can only be decrypted by the Ultravisor firmware.

## Prerequisites

- Machine with Protected Virtualization feature (stfle bit 158)
- `prot_virt=1` on host kernel command line
- KVM hypervisor required
- `KVM_CAP_S390_PROTECTED` capability

## Running a PVM

Select CPU with `Unpack facility` (stfle bit 161) and add:

```
-object s390-pv-guest,id=pv0 \
-machine confidential-guest-support=pv0
```

This ensures the `unpack` facility is available, enables IOMMU by default, and initializes the PV mechanism.

## Boot Process

Secure guest images can be loaded from disk (using s390-ccw BIOS) or supplied via `-kernel`. The secure image has a stage3a component that uses diag308 subcodes 8 and 10 to trigger secure mode transition.

Use `genprotimg` from s390-tools to prepare PVM images.
ENDOFFILE)
