# Banana Pi BPI-M2U (`bpim2u`)

Banana Pi BPI-M2 Ultra is a quad-core mini single board computer built with Allwinner A40i/R40/V40 SoC. It features 2GB of RAM and 8GB eMMC with onboard WiFi and BT.

## Supported devices

- SMP (Quad Core Cortex-A7)
- Generic Interrupt Controller configuration
- SRAM mappings
- SDRAM controller
- Timer device (re-used from Allwinner A10)
- UART
- SD/MMC storage controller
- EMAC ethernet
- GMAC ethernet
- Clock Control Unit
- SATA
- TWI (I2C)
- USB 2.0
- Hardware Watchdog

## Limitations

- Graphical output via HDMI, GPU and/or the Display Engine
- Audio output
- Real Time Clock

## Boot options

### Running mainline Linux

```bash
$ ARCH=arm CROSS_COMPILE=arm-linux-gnueabi- make sunxi_defconfig
$ qemu-system-arm -M bpim2u -nographic \
    -kernel /path/to/linux/arch/arm/boot/zImage \
    -append 'console=ttyS0,115200' \
    -dtb /path/to/linux/arch/arm/boot/dts/sun8i-r40-bananapi-m2-ultra.dtb
```

### Running U-Boot

```bash
$ dd if=/dev/zero of=sd.img bs=32M count=1
$ dd if=u-boot-sunxi-with-spl.bin of=sd.img bs=1k seek=8 conv=notrunc
$ qemu-system-arm -M bpim2u -nographic -sd sd.img
```
