title: "microvm Virtual Platform"
source: "system/i386/microvm.rst"
---

# microvm Virtual Platform

`microvm` is a machine type inspired by Firecracker and constructed after its machine model. It's a minimalist machine type without PCI nor ACPI support, designed for short-lived guests.

## Supported Devices

- ISA bus
- i8259 PIC (optional)
- i8254 PIT (optional)
- MC146818 RTC (optional)
- One ISA serial port (optional)
- LAPIC
- IOAPIC (with kernel-irqchip=split by default)
- kvmclock (if using KVM)
- fw_cfg
- Up to eight virtio-mmio devices

## Limitations

- No PCI-only devices
- No hotplug of any kind
- No live migration across QEMU versions

## Machine-Specific Options

- `microvm.x-option-roms=bool` - Disable option ROMs
- `microvm.pit=OnOffAuto` - Enable i8254 PIT
- `microvm.isa-serial=bool` - Disable ISA serial port
- `microvm.pic=OnOffAuto` - Enable i8259 PIC
- `microvm.rtc=OnOffAuto` - Enable MC146818 RTC
- `microvm.auto-kernel-cmdline=bool` - Disable auto kernel cmdline

## Boot Options

By default uses `qboot` BIOS, also compatible with `SeaBIOS`. Needs host-side kernel boot.

## Example (Maximum Compatibility)

```
$ qemu-system-x86_64 -M microvm \
   -enable-kvm -cpu host -m 512m -smp 2 \
   -kernel vmlinux -append "earlyprintk=ttyS0 console=ttyS0 root=/dev/vda" \
   -nodefaults -no-user-config -nographic \
   -serial stdio \
   -drive id=test,file=test.img,format=raw,if=none \
   -device virtio-blk-device,drive=test \
   -netdev tap,id=tap0,script=no,downscript=no \
   -device virtio-net-device,netdev=tap0
```

## Example (Minimal Footprint)

```
$ qemu-system-x86_64 \
   -M microvm,x-option-roms=off,pit=off,pic=off,isa-serial=off,rtc=off \
   -enable-kvm -cpu host -m 512m -smp 2 \
   -kernel vmlinux -append "console=hvc0 root=/dev/vda" \
   -nodefaults -no-user-config -nographic \
   -chardev stdio,id=virtiocon0 \
   -device virtio-serial-device \
   -device virtconsole,chardev=virtiocon0
```

## Guest-Initiated Shutdown

Use `triple-fault` mechanism. Add `reboot=t` to kernel command line for fastest shutdown.
ENDOFFILE
echo "Done: i386/microvm.md")
