title: "Xen PVH Machine"
source: "system/i386/xenpvh.rst"
---

# Xen PVH Machine (xenpvh)

PVH is a mode that uses HW virtualization features (like HVM) but avoids emulation models and instead uses passthrough or paravirtualized devices.

QEMU provides PV virtio devices on an emulated PCIe controller for this minimal machine.

## Supported Devices

- RAM
- GPEX host bridge
- virtio-pci devices

Any compatible PCI device model will work depending on Xen and guest support.

## Example

```
qemu-system-i386 -xen-domid 3 -no-shutdown \
  -chardev socket,id=libxl-cmd,path=/var/run/xen/qmp-libxl-3,server=on,wait=off \
  -mon chardev=libxl-cmd,mode=control \
  -nodefaults -no-user-config -xen-attach -name g0 \
  -vnc none -display none \
  -device virtio-net-pci,id=nic0,netdev=net0,mac=00:16:3e:5c:81:78 \
  -netdev type=tap,id=net0,ifname=vif3.0-emu,br=xenbr0,script=no,downscript=no \
  -smp 4,maxcpus=4 -nographic \
  -machine xenpvh \
  -m 4096
```
ENDOFFILE
