# Orange Pi PC (`orangepi-pc`)

The Xunlong Orange Pi PC is an Allwinner H3 SoC based embedded computer with mainline U-Boot and Linux support. Quad Core Cortex-A7 @ 1.3GHz, 1GiB RAM, 100Mbit ethernet.

## Supported devices

- SMP (Quad Core Cortex-A7), GIC, SRAM, SDRAM controller
- Real Time Clock, Timer, UART, SD/MMC
- EMAC ethernet, USB 2.0, Clock Control Unit
- System Control, Security Identifier, TWI (I2C), Watchdog

## Limitations

- Graphical output via HDMI, GPU and/or Display Engine
- Audio output
- Hardware Watchdog

## Machine-specific options

- `allwinner-rtc.base-year=YYYY` - Override RTC base year (minimum 1900)
- `allwinner-sid.identifier=...` - Security Identifier value

## Running mainline Linux

```bash
$ ARCH=arm CROSS_COMPILE=arm-linux-gnueabi- make sunxi_defconfig
$ qemu-system-arm -M orangepi-pc -nic user -nographic \
    -kernel /path/to/linux/arch/arm/boot/zImage \
    -append 'console=ttyS0,115200' \
    -dtb /path/to/linux/arch/arm/boot/dts/sun8i-h3-orangepi-pc.dtb
```

## Running U-Boot

```bash
$ qemu-system-arm -M orangepi-pc -nic user -nographic \
    -kernel /path/to/uboot/u-boot -sd disk.img
```

## Running NetBSD

NetBSD 9.0 works best. Get the `evbarm-earmv7hf` image and install U-Boot:

```bash
$ gunzip armv7.img.gz
$ dd if=/path/to/u-boot-sunxi-with-spl.bin of=armv7.img bs=1024 seek=8 conv=notrunc
$ qemu-img resize armv7.img 2G
$ qemu-system-arm -M orangepi-pc -nic user -nographic \
      -sd armv7.img -global allwinner-rtc.base-year=2000
```
ENDOFFILE)
