# RISC-V System Emulator

QEMU RISC-V system emulator supporting 32-bit and 64-bit RISC-V processors.

## Board Selection

For general-purpose use, the **virt** virtual platform is recommended. It provides:

- VirtIO devices (net, block, console, GPU, input)
- PLIC interrupt controller
- CLINT timer
- PCI bus (64-bit only)

For specific hardware emulation, use the corresponding board (SiFive, Microchip, etc.).

## Supported Machines

See individual board pages:

- [virt](riscv/virt.md) - Generic virtual platform (recommended)
- [SiFive Unleashed](riscv/sifive_u.md) - HiFive Unleashed
- [Microchip Icicle Kit](riscv/microchip-icicle-kit.md) - PolarFire SoC
- [MicroBlaze V](riscv/microblaze-v-generic.md) - AMD MicroBlaze V
- [Shakti C](riscv/shakti-c.md) - Shakti reference platform
- [XiangShan Kunminghu](riscv/xiangshan-kunminghu.md) - FPGA prototype
- [MIPS RISC-V](riscv/mips.md) - MIPS RISC-V processors

## Firmware Options

- **OpenSBI**: Default firmware for M-mode boot
- **U-Boot**: Supported as payload or first-stage
- **Direct kernel**: Use `-kernel` to boot directly

## Usage

```
qemu-system-riscv64 -machine virt -kernel Image
qemu-system-riscv32 -machine virt -kernel Image
```
ENDOFFILE)
