# Arm Server Base System Architecture Reference board (`sbsa-ref`)

The `sbsa-ref` board intends to look like real hardware (while `virt` is a generic platform). Defined by:

- [Base System Architecture (BSA)](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/den0094/)
- [Server Base System Architecture (SBSA)](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/den0029/)
- [Arm Base Boot Requirements (BBR)](https://developer.arm.com/documentation/den0044/)

## Supported devices

- Configurable number of AArch64 CPUs
- GIC version 3
- System bus AHCI controller, XHCI controller
- CDROM and hard disc on AHCI bus
- E1000E ethernet card on PCIe bus
- Bochs display adapter on PCIe bus
- Generic SBSA watchdog device

## Board to firmware interface

`sbsa-ref` is a static system that reports a minimal devicetree to firmware for non-discoverable information. This devicetree reports CPUs, memory, platform version, GIC addresses, NUMA node id, and CPU topology.

## Platform version

- 0.0 - Devicetree holds CPUs, memory and platform version
- 0.1 - GIC information present
- 0.2 - GIC ITS information present
- 0.3 - USB controller is XHCI (not EHCI)
- 0.4 - CPU topology information present
ENDOFFILE)
