# QEMU Monitor

The QEMU monitor is used to give complex commands to the QEMU emulator. You can use it to:

- Remove or insert removable media images (such as CD-ROM or floppies)
- Freeze/unfreeze the Virtual Machine (VM) and save or restore its state from a disk file
- Inspect the VM state without an external debugger

## Commands

See the QEMU documentation for the full list of available HMP commands and info commands.

## Integer Expressions

The monitor understands integer expressions for every integer argument. You can use register names to get the value of specific CPU registers by prefixing them with `$`.
ENDOFFILE
