# vhost-user-gpu Protocol

> Source: `docs/interop/vhost-user-gpu.rst`

## Overview

vhost-user-gpu is a protocol extension for GPU device backends, supporting virtio-gpu devices with display and cursor functionality.

## Message Types

| ID | Name | Description |
|----|------|-------------|
| 1 | GET_EDID | Get EDID data for a display |
| 2 | UPDATE_SCANOUT | Update scanout (display) configuration |
| 3 | UPDATE_CURSOR | Update cursor position/image |
| 4 | DMABUF_DMABUF | DMA-BUF operations |

## Scanout Configuration

The UPDATE_SCANOUT message configures display outputs with fields: `scanout_id`, `x`, `y`, `w`, `h`, `format`, `stride`, `offset`.

## Cursor Updates

The UPDATE_CURSOR message handles cursor rendering with fields: `scanout_id`, `x`, `y`, `hot_x`, `hot_y`, `width`, `height`, `format`.

## Supported Formats

- VIRTIO_GPU_FORMAT_B8G8R8X8_UNORM
- VIRTIO_GPU_FORMAT_B8G8R8A8_UNORM
- VIRTIO_GPU_FORMAT_R8G8B8X8_UNORM
- VIRTIO_GPU_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM

## See Also

- [vhost-user protocol](vhost-user.md)
- virtio-gpu specification
ENDOFFILE
