# VNC LED State Pseudo-Encoding

> Source: `docs/interop/vnc-ledstate-pseudo-encoding.rst`

## Overview

The VNC LED state pseudo-encoding allows the server to communicate keyboard LED states (Caps Lock, Num Lock, Scroll Lock) to the client.

- **Encoding number**: -261
- **Direction**: Server to Client

## LED State Format

A single byte with 3 bits:

| Bit | LED | Description |
|-----|-----|-------------|
| 0 | Scroll Lock | 1 = on, 0 = off |
| 1 | Num Lock | 1 = on, 0 = off |
| 2 | Caps Lock | 1 = on, 0 = off |

## Protocol Flow

1. Client advertises support for encoding -261 in SetEncodings
2. Server sends current LED state immediately after encoding is enabled
3. Server sends updates when LED state changes

## See Also

- VNC protocol specification
- QEMU VNC server documentation
ENDOFFILE
