# S390x System Emulator

QEMU S/390 system emulator for IBM Z mainframe architecture.

## Overview

The S/390 system emulator provides full system emulation of IBM Z hardware, supporting Linux guests with full I/O virtualization.

## Key Features

- **Processor**: z/Architecture with multiple CPU generations
- **Memory**: Up to several TB depending on guest configuration
- **I/O**: Channel subsystem with virtio and vfio-ccw passthrough
- **Virtualization**: Protected Virtualization (PV) support

## Related Pages

- [3270 Terminal Devices](s390x/3270.md)
- [Boot Devices](s390x/bootdevices.md)
- [CPU Topology](s390x/cpu-topology.md)
- [Channel Subsystem](s390x/css.md)
- [PCI Devices](s390x/pcidevices.md)
- [Protected Virtualization](s390x/protvirt.md)
- [VFIO-AP](s390x/vfio-ap.md)
- [VFIO-CCW](s390x/vfio-ccw.md)

## Usage

```
qemu-system-s390x -machine s390-ccw-virtio -m 2G -kernel bzImage
```
ENDOFFILE)
