# TLS Setup for QEMU

How to configure TLS (Transport Layer Security) for QEMU network and VNC connections.

## Overview

QEMU supports TLS encryption for:
- VNC connections
- NBD (Network Block Device) connections
- Character devices

TLS uses X.509 certificates for authentication and encryption.

## Certificate Setup

### Creating a Certificate Authority (CA)

Generate a CA key and certificate:

```bash
certtool --generate-privkey > ca-key.pem
certtool --generate-self-signed --load-privkey ca-key.pem \
         --template ca.info --outfile ca-cert.pem
```

### Creating Server Certificates

```bash
certtool --generate-privkey > server-key.pem
certtool --generate-certificate --load-privkey server-key.pem \
         --load-ca-certificate ca-cert.pem --load-ca-privkey ca-key.pem \
         --template server.info --outfile server-cert.pem
```

### Creating Client Certificates (optional)

```bash
certtool --generate-privkey > client-key.pem
certtool --generate-certificate --load-privkey client-key.pem \
         --load-ca-certificate ca-cert.pem --load-ca-privkey ca-key.pem \
         --template client.info --outfile client-cert.pem
```

## Using TLS Credentials in QEMU

### As a Server (e.g., VNC)

```
qemu-system-x86_64 -vnc :0,tls-creds=tls0 \
    -object tls-creds-x509,id=tls0,dir=/etc/pki/qemu,endpoint=server
```

### As a Client (NBD)

```
qemu-system-x86_64 -drive file=nbd:server:port,tls-creds=tls0 \
    -object tls-creds-x509,id=tls0,dir=/etc/pki/qemu,endpoint=client
```

## PSK (Pre-Shared Keys)

For simpler setups without certificates:

```
-object tls-creds-psk,id=tls0,dir=/etc/qemu/psk,endpoint=server,username=user
```

## Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC)

QEMU supports post-quantum TLS algorithms for future-proof security. Enable with appropriate GnuTLS configuration.
ENDOFFILE)
