# Aspeed family boards

The QEMU Aspeed machines model BMCs of various OpenPOWER systems and Aspeed evaluation boards. They are based on different releases of the Aspeed SoC: AST2400 (ARM926EJ-S 400MHz), AST2500 (ARM1176JZS 800MHz), AST2600 (dual Cortex-A7 1.2GHz).

## AST2400 SoC based machines

- `palmetto-bmc` - OpenPOWER Palmetto POWER8 BMC
- `quanta-q71l-bmc` - OpenBMC Quanta BMC
- `supermicrox11-bmc` - Supermicro X11 BMC
- `supermicrox11spi-bmc` - Supermicro X11 SPI BMC

## AST2500 SoC based machines

- `ast2500-evb` - Aspeed AST2500 Evaluation board
- `romulus-bmc` - OpenPOWER Romulus POWER9 BMC
- `witherspoon-bmc` - OpenPOWER Witherspoon POWER9 BMC
- `g220a-bmc` - Bytedance G220A BMC
- `yosemitev2-bmc` - Facebook YosemiteV2 BMC
- `tiogapass-bmc` - Facebook Tiogapass BMC

## AST2600 SoC based machines

- `ast2600-evb` - Aspeed AST2600 Evaluation board (Cortex-A7)
- `rainier-bmc` - IBM Rainier POWER10 BMC
- `fuji-bmc` - Facebook Fuji BMC
- `bletchley-bmc` - Facebook Bletchley BMC
- `fby35-bmc` - Facebook fby35 BMC
- `gb200nvl-bmc` - Nvidia GB200nvl BMC

## Supported devices

- SMP (AST2600 Cortex-A7)
- Interrupt Controller (VIC), Timer, RTC
- I2C Controller, System Control Unit (SCU)
- SRAM, X-DMA, Static Memory Controller (SPI Flash)
- SPI Memory Controller, USB 2.0, SD/MMC
- SDRAM controller, Watchdog, GPIO, UART
- Ethernet controllers, Front LEDs (PCA9552)
- LPC Peripheral Controller
- Hash/Crypto Engine (HACE) - Hash only
- ADC, Secure Boot Controller (AST2600)
- eMMC Boot Controller, PECI, I3C, Internal Bridge

## Missing devices

- Coprocessor, PWM/Fan, Slave GPIO, Super I/O
- PCI-Express, Graphic Display, MCTP, Mailbox
- Virtual UART, eSPI

## Boot options

### From kernel image

```bash
$ qemu-system-arm -M ast2600-evb -nographic \
      -kernel arch/arm/boot/zImage \
      -dtb arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed-ast2600-evb.dtb \
      -initrd rootfs.cpio
```

### From flash image

```bash
$ qemu-system-arm -M romulus-bmc -nic user \
    -drive file=obmc-phosphor-image-romulus.static.mtd,format=raw,if=mtd -nographic
```

### From eMMC image

```bash
$ qemu-system-arm -M rainier-bmc \
      -drive file=mmc.img,format=raw,if=sd,index=2 \
      -nographic
```

## Aspeed 2700 family boards

AST2700 with quad cores Arm Cortex-A35 64 bits CPUs (1.6GHz).

- `ast2700-evb` - Aspeed AST2700 Evaluation board
- `ast2700fc` - Aspeed AST2700 Evaluation board (Cortex-A35 + Cortex-M4)

## Aspeed MiniBMC family boards

Based on AST1030/AST1060 with Arm Cortex M4F CPU (200MHz).

- `ast1030-evb` - Aspeed AST1030 Evaluation board
- `ast1060-evb` - Aspeed AST1060 Evaluation board
ENDOFFILE)
