# Arm MPS2 and MPS3 boards

The Arm MPS2, MPS2+ and MPS3 dev boards are FPGA based. QEMU models the following FPGA images:

## M-profile CPUs

- `mps2-an385` - Cortex-M3 (AN385)
- `mps2-an386` - Cortex-M4 (AN386)
- `mps2-an500` - Cortex-M7 (AN500)
- `mps2-an505` - Cortex-M33 (AN505)
- `mps2-an511` - Cortex-M3 DesignStart (AN511)
- `mps2-an521` - Dual Cortex-M33 (AN521)
- `mps3-an524` - Dual Cortex-M33 on MPS3 (AN524)
- `mps3-an547` - Cortex-M55 on MPS3 (AN547)

## R-profile CPUs

- `mps3-an536` - Dual Cortex-R52 on MPS3 (AN536)

## Differences from real hardware

- AN385/AN386 remapping of low 16K memory unimplemented
- AN524 remapping of low memory to BRAM/QSPI flash unimplemented
- QEMU provides LAN9118 ethernet rather than LAN9220
- QSPI flash modeled as simple ROM on MPS3 boards
- USB controller not modeled on MPS3 boards
- AN536 does not support runtime CPU reset/halt control via SCC
- AN536 defaults to single CPU; use `-smp 2` for second CPU

## Machine-specific options

For `mps3-an524`:
- `remap` - Set `BRAM`/`QSPI` to select initial memory mapping (default: `BRAM`)
ENDOFFILE)
