# Nuvoton iBMC boards

The [Nuvoton iBMC](https://www.nuvoton.com/products/cloud-computing/ibmc/) chips are Arm-based SoCs designed for Baseboard Management Controllers (BMCs) in servers.

## NPCM7XX series (Cortex-A9)

- `npcm750-evb` - Nuvoton NPCM750 Evaluation board
- `quanta-gbs-bmc` - Quanta GBS server BMC
- `quanta-gsj` - Quanta GSJ server BMC
- `kudo-bmc` - Fii USA Kudo server BMC
- `mori-bmc` - Fii USA Mori server BMC

## NPCM8XX series (Cortex-A35)

- `npcm845-evb` - Nuvoton NPCM845 Evaluation board

## Supported devices

- SMP (Dual Core Cortex-A9), SCU, GIC, Global Timer, Private Timer/Watchdog
- SRAM, ROM, DRAM, GCR, CLK, TIM
- Serial ports (16550-based), DDR4 controller
- OTP, FIU (SPI Flash), RNG, USB host
- GPIO, ADC, PWM, SMBus, EMC Ethernet
- Tachometer, PSPI

## Missing devices

- LPC/eSPI host-to-BMC interface (KBCI, KCS, POST code, SWC, SHM, eSPI slave)
- GMAC, USBD, SD/MMC, PECI, PCI/PCIe
- VDM/MCTP, Serial I/O, Graphics, Video
- I3C (8XX), Temperature sensor (8XX), Virtual UART (8XX)

## Boot options

```bash
$ qemu-system-arm -machine quanta-gsj -nographic \
    -drive file=image-bmc,if=mtd,bus=0,unit=0,format=raw
```

Default root password for test images: `0penBmc`
ENDOFFILE)
